sections.s5b_flow:
```
  ═══ try-with-resources FLOW ═══

  try (Resource r = new Resource()) {
      use(r);       ← success or exception
  }
  ↓ try exits (any reason)
  r.close();        ← AUTOMATIC! Always called.

  ═══ MULTIPLE RESOURCES ═══

  try (Connection conn = getConn();
       Statement stmt = conn.stmt();
       ResultSet rs = stmt.query()) {
      use(rs);
  }
  Close order: rs → stmt → conn (REVERSE of declaration)

  ═══ SUPPRESSED EXCEPTIONS ═══

  try body throws: RuntimeException("MAIN")     ← PRIMARY
  resource.close() throws: Exception("CLOSE")   ← SUPPRESSED
  Caller catches: RuntimeException with getSuppressed() = [Exception("CLOSE")]
  BOTH visible! Unlike finally-throw which SWALLOWS.

  ═══ BEFORE vs AFTER ═══

  BEFORE (finally): 12 lines, null checks, nested try-catch
  AFTER (try-with-resources): 4 lines, auto-close, clean
```
